 "internal_silences": [],
 "text": "Some decisions are easy, and some keep us awake at night. For the difficult ones, I follow a short method. First, I write the question at the top of a page. Then I list the options, even the ones that seem unlikely. For each option, I note the main benefit and the main risk. Next, I ask what I would advise a friend to do. This simple question often makes the answer clear. If the answer is still not clear, I wait one more day. A good night of sleep can change how a problem looks. Most decisions are not final, and it is usually possible to adjust the plan later if needed."
